{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++14 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++14 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nThe leader of some very secretive organization has decided to invite all other members to a meeting. All members of the organization live in the same town which can be represented as $$$n$$$ crossroads connected by $$$m$$$ two-directional streets. The meeting will be held in the leader's house near the crossroad $$$1$$$. There are $$$k$$$ members of the organization invited to the meeting; $$$i$$$-th of them lives near the crossroad $$$a_i$$$. All members of the organization receive the message about the meeting at the same moment and start moving to the location where the meeting is held. In the beginning of each minute each person is located at some crossroad. He or she can either wait a minute at this crossroad, or spend a minute to walk from the current crossroad along some street to another crossroad (obviously, it is possible to start walking along the street only if it begins or ends at the current crossroad). In the beginning of the first minute each person is at the crossroad where he or she lives. As soon as a person reaches the crossroad number $$$1$$$, he or she immediately comes to the leader's house and attends the meeting.Obviously, the leader wants all other members of the organization to come up as early as possible. But, since the organization is very secretive, the leader does not want to attract much attention. Let's denote the discontent of the leader as follows  initially the discontent is $$$0$$$;  whenever a person reaches the crossroad number $$$1$$$, the discontent of the leader increases by $$$c \\cdot x$$$, where $$$c$$$ is some fixed constant, and $$$x$$$ is the number of minutes it took the person to reach the crossroad number $$$1$$$;  whenever $$$x$$$ members of the organization walk along the same street at the same moment in the same direction, $$$dx^2$$$ is added to the discontent, where $$$d$$$ is some fixed constant. This is not cumulative: for example, if two persons are walking along the same street in the same direction at the same moment, then $$$4d$$$ is added to the discontent, not $$$5d$$$. Before sending a message about the meeting, the leader can tell each member of the organization which path they should choose and where they should wait. Help the leader to establish a plan for every member of the organization so they all reach the crossroad $$$1$$$, and the discontent is minimized.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++14 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i128 = __int128_t;\nusing i64 = long long;\nusing f80 = long double;\nusing pt = complex<i64>;\n\ntemplate<typename F, typename C>\nstruct MCF {\n    struct Edge {\n        int u, v;\n        F cap, flow;\n        C cost;\n        int rev;\n    };\n\n    int n;\n    vector<vector<Edge>> g;\n    vector<C> dist, pot;\n    vector<Edge*> prev_edge;\n\n    MCF(int N) : n(N), g(N), dist(N), pot(N), prev_edge(N) {}\n\n    void add(int u, int v, F c, C w) {\n        g[u].push_back({u, v, c, 0, w, (int)g[v].size()});\n        if (u == v) g[u].back().rev++;\n        g[v].push_back({v, u, 0, 0, -w, (int)g[u].size() - 1});\n    }\n\n    bool dijkstra(int s, int t) {\n        fill(dist.begin(), dist.end(), numeric_limits<C>::max());\n        fill(prev_edge.begin(), prev_edge.end(), nullptr);\n        dist[s] = 0;\n\n        using P = pair<C, int>;\n        priority_queue<P, vector<P>, greater<P>> pq;\n        pq.emplace(0, s);\n\n        while (!pq.empty()) {\n            auto [d, u] = pq.top(); pq.pop();\n            if (d != dist[u]) continue;\n\n            for (auto &e : g[u]) {\n                if (e.flow < e.cap &&\n                    dist[e.v] > dist[u] + e.cost + pot[u] - pot[e.v]) {\n                    dist[e.v] = dist[u] + e.cost + pot[u] - pot[e.v];\n                    prev_edge[e.v] = &e;\n                    pq.emplace(dist[e.v], e.v);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return dist[t] < numeric_limits<C>::max();\n    }\n\n    pair<F, C> run(int s, int t) {\n        F total_flow = 0;\n        C total_cost = 0;\n\n        fill(pot.begin(), pot.end(), 0);\n        while (dijkstra(s, t)) {\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n                if (dist[i] < numeric_limits<C>::max())\n                    pot[i] += dist[i];\n\n            F delta = numeric_limits<F>::max();\n            for (Edge *e = prev_edge[t]; e; e = prev_edge[e->u])\n                delta = min(delta, e->cap - e->flow);\n\n            for (Edge *e = prev_edge[t]; e; e = prev_edge[e->u]) {\n                e->flow += delta;\n                g[e->v][e->rev].flow -= delta;\n                total_cost += delta * e->cost;\n            }\n            total_flow += delta;\n        }\n        return {total_flow, total_cost};\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int N, M, K, C, D;\n    cin >> N >> M >> K >> C >> D;\n\n    vector<int> cnt(N + 1, 0);\n    for (int i = 0, x; i < K; ++i) {\n        cin >> x;\n        ++cnt[x];\n    }\n\n    int sink = (K + 1) * N * N + 1;\n    MCF<int, int> mcf(sink + 1);\n\n    for (int i = 0, u, v; i < M; ++i) {\n        cin >> u >> v;\n        for (int t = 0; t < K * N; ++t) {\n            for (int j = 1; j <= 1 + 2 * K; j += 2) {\n                mcf.add(t * N + u, (t + 1) * N + v, 1, j * D + C);\n                mcf.add(t * N + v, (t + 1) * N + u, 1, j * D + C);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    for (int t = 0; t < K * N; ++t) {\n        for (int j = 1; j <= N; ++j) {\n            mcf.add(t * N + j, (t + 1) * N + j, K, C);\n        }\n    }\n\n    for (int t = 0; t <= K * N; ++t) {\n        mcf.add(t * N + 1, sink, K, 0);\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 1; i <= N; ++i) {\n        if (cnt[i] > 0) {\n            mcf.add(0, i, cnt[i], 0);\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << mcf.run(0, sink).second << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\nusing f80 = long double;\n\ntemplate<typename F, typename C>\nstruct MCF {\n    struct Edge {\n        int u, v;\n        F cap, flow;\n        C cost;\n        int rev;\n    };\n\n    int n;\n    vector<vector<Edge>> g;\n    vector<C> dist, pot;\n    vector<Edge*> prev_edge;\n\n    MCF(int N) : n(N), g(N), dist(N), pot(N), prev_edge(N) {}\n\n    void add(int u, int v, F c, C w) {\n        g[u].push_back({u, v, c, 0, w, (int)g[v].size()});\n        if (u == v) g[u].back().rev++;\n        g[v].push_back({v, u, 0, 0, -w, (int)g[u].size() - 1});\n    }\n\n    bool dijkstra(int s, int t) {\n        fill(dist.begin(), dist.end(), numeric_limits<C>::max());\n        fill(prev_edge.begin(), prev_edge.end(), nullptr);\n        dist[s] = 0;\n\n        using P = pair<C, int>;\n        priority_queue<P, vector<P>, greater<P>> pq;\n        pq.emplace(0, s);\n\n        while (!pq.empty()) {\n            auto [d, u] = pq.top(); pq.pop();\n            if (d != dist[u]) continue;\n\n            for (auto &e : g[u]) {\n                if (e.flow < e.cap &&\n                    dist[e.v] > dist[u] + e.cost + pot[u] - pot[e.v]) {\n                    dist[e.v] = dist[u] + e.cost + pot[u] - pot[e.v];\n                    prev_edge[e.v] = &e;\n                    pq.emplace(dist[e.v], e.v);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return dist[t] < numeric_limits<C>::max();\n    }\n\n    pair<F, C> run(int s, int t) {\n        F total_flow = 0;\n        C total_cost = 0;\n\n        fill(pot.begin(), pot.end(), 0);\n        while (dijkstra(s, t)) {\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n                if (dist[i] < numeric_limits<C>::max())\n                    pot[i] += dist[i];\n\n            F delta = numeric_limits<F>::max();\n            for (Edge *e = prev_edge[t]; e; e = prev_edge[e->u])\n                delta = min(delta, e->cap - e->flow);\n\n            for (Edge *e = prev_edge[t]; e; e = prev_edge[e->u]) {\n                e->flow += delta;\n                g[e->v][e->rev].flow -= delta;\n                total_cost += delta * e->cost;\n            }\n            total_flow += delta;\n        }\n        return {total_flow, total_cost};\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int N, M, K, C, D;\n    cin >> N >> M >> K >> C >> D;\n\n    vector<int> cnt(N + 1, 0);\n    for (int i = 0, x; i < K; ++i) {\n        cin >> x;\n        ++cnt[x];\n    }\n\n    // Build graph with time-expanded network\n    // We'll use a maximum time bound of K*N minutes\n    int max_time = K * N + 1;\n    int sink = N * max_time + 1;\n    MCF<int, int> mcf(sink + 1);\n\n    // Add edges for each street for each time step\n    for (int i = 0; i < M; ++i) {\n        int u, v;\n        cin >> u >> v;\n        --u; --v;\n        for (int t = 0; t < max_time - 1; ++t) {\n            // For each person using the street at time t, cost is (2*person_count-1)*D + C\n            // But we use multiple edges to model the quadratic cost\n            for (int j = 1; j <= K; ++j) {\n                mcf.add(t * N + u, (t + 1) * N + v, 1, (2 * j - 1) * D + C);\n                mcf.add(t * N + v, (t + 1) * N + u, 1, (2 * j - 1) * D + C);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Add waiting edges\n    for (int t = 0; t < max_time - 1; ++t) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < N; ++j) {\n            for (int k = 1; k <= K; ++k) {\n                mcf.add(t * N + j, (t + 1) * N + j, 1, (2 * k - 1) * D + C);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Add edges from node 1 (destination) to sink at all times\n    for (int t = 0; t < max_time; ++t) {\n        mcf.add(t * N + 0, sink, K, 0);\n    }\n\n    // Add edges from source to starting positions\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n        if (cnt[i + 1] > 0) {\n            mcf.add(sink + 1, i * N + i, cnt[i + 1], 0);\n        }\n    }\n\n    auto result = mcf.run(sink + 1, sink);\n    cout << result.second << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.622600959512056e-06, -3.93382906622719e-05, -3.814689989667386e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.962863310240209e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.792098479811102e-05, -2.8609820219571702e-05, -1.4185804502631072e-05, -2.622600959512056e-06, -1.490105023549404e-05, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -4.172316494077677e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.0013872295385226607, -0.0895102471113205, -0.17976118624210358, -5.960462772236497e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -6.198863957251888e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.1128237321972847, -0.00039986721822060645, -0.36490190029144287, -0.002618576865643263, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.0609570381348021e-05, -3.8742269680369645e-05, -0.1269301474094391, -0.14646446704864502, -0.0001731960946926847, -0.00993367936462164, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -0.0013430631952360272, -5.006777428206988e-06, -8.177422569133341e-05, -4.160317621426657e-05, -0.000658891047